   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div>Hello,<div dir=\"auto\">This is a warning, not an error. For species GEOFFROY, bandwidth estimation (of the kernel density) failed. This usually happens when there are too few records, or multiple records are at the same time. </div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">I doubt this has to do with the date format. It&#39;s just that the data for species may not be suitable for density estimation.</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">If you have multiple records at different times and still get that error please provide a reproducible example. </div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">Thank you,</div><div dir=\"auto\">Jürgen </div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
